<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chapter-3-intro">
  <title>Week 3</title>
  <introduction>

    <p>
      At the end of this week you should be able to...
    </p>
    <objectives>
      <ul>
        <li>Use appropriate terminology to identify and describe components of classes</li>
        <li>Describe values (instances) of custom class types</li>
        <li>Illustrate the scope of variables and visibility within classes in Java</li>
        <li>Compose a simple class through design, implementation, and testing to meet behavioral requirements</li>
        <li>Develop programs that create simple classes and instantiate objects of those classes</li>
      </ul>
    </objectives>
  </introduction>
  
  
  <xi:include href="sec-programming-paradigms.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-class-design-basics.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-string-operations.ptx"/>
</chapter>

